lstc offers various types OTB (out-the-box), here is just a part of them
Map (slow lookup, kv storage)
UMap (unordered map, fast, same kv)
syntax for map:
let: (map type)<type -> type> name = {a: b, c:d, e : f}; /-/ aka any spacing
Vector - dynamic array
Set
int -
subtypes :
u(8/16/32/64)
i(8/16/32/64)
if you use int, you actually make i32, to use another type, just use it directly
float:
f(32/64)
/-/ string - automatically managed string : deprecated, now will be provided by lstclib
char
double - virtualized 128 bit /-/ idk, can be discarded or implemented way later (too hard)
bool
none (like void in C)

arrays:
let: type name[n]
